From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SushyDev <mail@sushy.dev>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:08:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: write the whole 128-byte PPS

msm_dp_panel_dsc_hw_config() wrote 22 words to the PPS store, described
as the 88-byte DSC 1.1 payload.  DSC 1.1 and 1.2 both define a 128-byte
picture parameter set, and the store is 32 words wide.

Words 22-31 kept whatever they held before.  Read back on hardware at
3440x1440@120 they were not zero:

  0x200 : 000000c0 00000001 00000010 00000011

so PPS byte 88, native_422_420, reached the sink as 0xc0 rather than 0.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
index 1b798ba..bade31a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
@@ -783,7 +783,7 @@ void msm_dp_panel_dsc_hw_config(struct msm_dp_panel *msm_dp_panel,
 	struct drm_dsc_picture_parameter_set pps;
 	const u8 *bytes;
 	u32 val, dto_count, bytes_per_line, parity_word;
-	u8 parity[24] = { 0 };
+	u8 parity[32] = { 0 };
 	int i;
 
 	if (!msm_dp_panel)
@@ -806,8 +806,7 @@ void msm_dp_panel_dsc_hw_config(struct msm_dp_panel *msm_dp_panel,
 	bytes = (const u8 *)&pps;
 	msm_dp_write_link(panel, DP_PPS_HB_0_3, 0x007F1000);
 	msm_dp_write_link(panel, DP_PPS_PB_0_3, 0x00A22300);
-	/* SM8550's DP PPS store carries the 88-byte DSC 1.1 payload. */
-	for (i = 0; i < 22; i++) {
+	for (i = 0; i < 32; i++) {
 		val = bytes[i * 4] | bytes[i * 4 + 1] << 8 |
 			bytes[i * 4 + 2] << 16 | bytes[i * 4 + 3] << 24;
 		msm_dp_write_link(panel, DP_PPS_PPS_0_3 + i * 4, val);
